<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/2nd-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marcomannic Wars</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">166–180</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century">2nd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Marcomannic Wars were a series of conflicts fought from about 166 to 180 CE between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a> and Germanic and Sarmatian peoples of the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a>, including the Marcomanni, Quadi and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iazyges">Iazyges</a>. They began with invasions that reached northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcus-aurelius">Marcus Aurelius</a> spent much of his reign on the frontier, and peace was concluded by his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/commodus">Commodus</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marcomannic-wars.jpg" alt="Marcomannic Wars" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nico Kokkonen · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Column_of_Marcus_Aurelius_-_detail4.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
